{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merged: terminable, fail-closed migration preconditions, on main at 6b69288d.\n\nThe quiet-wave gate that releases the dot-artifact migration could neither reach zero nor be trusted when it did.\n\nIt counted every ratified approval, stale and retired included. `gs merge` refuses those, so a head held up by one is waiting for a fresh review rather than a merger, and waiting longer never clears it — a gate on an irreversible step that cannot reach zero either blocks for ever or teaches the operator to bypass it. It also recognised a verdict by filtering statements for a report with an approved body, which includes reports the fold refused, and keyed settlement by artifact so one chain's verdict settled every other request naming the same artifact. Together those hid five review requests that no effective verdict binds.\n\nSettlement now reads the effective review projection and binds through each request's own commitment chain, and the approved-head check counts only approvals a merger could still act on.\n\nThe page also states, where the retire rule is given, that live means not retired and that stale is a separate fact. That is the trap which produced a false all-clear on this very branch: I queried for artifacts that were neither retired nor stale, missed three that were stale-but-not-retired, and reported the path clear while they occupied it.\n\nSuccessor to 4f86c416, the reviewed branch artifact. This merge changed AGENTS.md and SKILL.md only; `make ui-check` is green and the embed is untouched, which I checked rather than assumed after the previous merge shipped an embed built from neither source.","body":{"commit":"6b69288de185123bf54a3d388bbb4d6db7561ddd","path":"AGENTS.md"}}